R4-Lite: pass the saved bootloader MAC to the LAN GMAC

U-Boot's fdt_fixup_ethernet() uses ethernet0 to copy ethaddr into the
Linux device tree. Without the alias, gmac0 falls back to a new random
address despite an existing saved ethaddr. Keep the configured WAN MAC
unchanged; this does not introduce a new address allocation policy.

--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-bananapi-bpi-r4-lite.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-bananapi-bpi-r4-lite.dts
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 		     "mediatek,mt7987a", "mediatek,mt7987";
 
 	aliases {
+		ethernet0 = &gmac0;
 		/* mt7987 I2C0 */
 		i2c0 = &i2c0;
 		/* PCA9548 (0-0070) provides 4 i2c channels */
